module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "an instrument label whose run executes the witness population and states, per identity, whether it is green at the default branch head and whether the required path runs it",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a witness red at origin/main has no row, so every PR that touches its module rediscovers and re-attributes it** (INVALID STATE: a committed witness fails under `gunbc run --claim-run` at the default branch head and nothing records that, which test, or whether the required path runs it).",

    "HARM: each lane has to re-measure the failure against main to show it is not its own, and a lane that skips the comparison either blames itself or absorbs the red. SPECIMEN (gunbc#14384, main 6ae9b3b9591, executed with `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <witness> --claim-run`): test.claim.rung_drop_superseded_standing_witness the_live_roster_loss_holders_resolve_and_stand; test.claim.compiler_frontend_program_status_witness every_declared_instrument_is_distinct_and_awaited; test.claim.exact_witness_admission_witness no_batch_mixes_a_pre_verdict_row_with_an_assertion_false_row and both_red_expectations_are_known_red_but_only_one_expects_a_pre_verdict_refusal. Whether any of the four is on the required path was not established by that lane.",

    "SPECIMEN, MECHANISM (D13, main 1acf79a8af4c, remote `claim_batch --claim-run` of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand_census with a probe printing `demand_census_row_line` per row): 14 of 22 claims FAIL on main, among them demand_through_a_transparent_callee_is_equal_holds, and the eight that pass are partly vacuous (their expected verdict is unobserved). THE REDUCER NEVER RAN, and a chain of unjustified links hid it, each behind the one before. LINK 1, STALE FIXTURE, FIXED: ddc_ingest omitted std.types while every fixture source imports `std.types { Bool }`, so 13 of 15 rows read unobserved resolve_module_not_found; the real std.types imports std.algebra, a world the fixture cannot supply, so the ingest carries a stub declaring `type Bool = True | False` exactly as dag/std/types.dag does. LINK 2, CENSUS DEFECT, FIXED: demand_census_authored_reading resolved a TYPE expression under the module-root value-category context, so since #14090 every `uses net: Network` was reference_category_mismatch, collapsed with three other arms into AuthoredTypeUnresolved; it now resolves under resolve_ctx_with_reference_category(TypeOccurrence) (v2.compiler.resolve unchanged; no other type-expression resolve_node site exists). LINK 3, CENSUS DEFECT, FIXED: since #14209 every list introduction heads with a generated reference to std.algebra.FreeMonoid and demand_fact_node counted it as a callee (callee_outside_closure at FreeMonoid); a list introduction is not a call, recognised by v2.std.list_introduction list_introduction_elements_optional, the reader eval uses. LINK 4, RESOLVED (two resolve defects, neither the fixture nor the walk; measured by remote probes on one `service H { operation Get { requires Network } }` module): every module with `import std.resources { Network }` and `requires Network` was REFUSED AT RESOLVE with resolve_reason_reference_category_mismatch at the requires member, so no OperationFact existed (census: function_not_declared, callee_outside_closure, empty vocabulary). Cause 1, v2.compiler.resolve: the arrow's resource-requirements slot walked in the ambient VALUE category although every member names a resource, which v2.std.symbol_index classifies TypeOccurrence; it now walks resolve_ctx_type_role. Cause 2, v2.std.symbol_index symbol_index_candidate_category: payload, namespace-body and resource marks are written at the DECLARING path but a candidate's path is the BINDING path, so an import binding read no mark; marks are now read at the binding's unique declaring path (symbol_index_candidate_marked_path; unavailable or contested keeps candidate.path, today's behaviour). Local resources worked only because binding path equals declaring path. REAL CORPUS: the same shape is 68 files (`import std.resources { Network }` then `requires Network`), e.g. dag/gunbc/auth/approval_ntfy_publish.dag operation Post and dag/extdeps/browser.dag, so real services were misread on the v2 native route; population measured by //gunbc/instruments:dependency-demand-census at the merge base and at the repair head. REASON COLLAPSE, STILL OPEN (a resolve_module_not_found refusal also carries an EMPTY unbound_locus): the four AuthoredTypeUnresolved arms (shell absent, lowering absent, resolve rejected, no declaration path) still print one cause; carrying resolve's reason in the row hit a closure-diagnostics cascade in which the record DemandCensusRow was erased to T (no field 'standings' on type 'T'), not yet reduced. AFTER LINKS 1-4 (remote claim_batch at the repair head): all 21 claims of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand_census PASS (the 22nd line counted earlier was the removed probe), every one of the nine link-4 fails now green; the 10 reducer claims of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand PASS (they were not exercised before); neighbours v2.test.claim.normalize.operation_requires_edge (15) and v2.test.claim.name_resolve.kind_aware_binding (21) PASS. Classification at claim identity: link 1 stale fixture, links 2-4 genuine defects in census and resolve, never environment-blocked. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT 1, mitigatable: the red is visible to whoever runs the witness and to no gate. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed for the enrolled population: a witness on the required path cannot be red at main because the merge queue refuses it; the unenrolled remainder is a ratchet.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: an instrument label whose run executes the witness population and states, per identity, whether it is green at the default branch head and whether the required path runs it. SUFFICIENT FOR: the four specimens above being counted, or shown absent, by that run rather than by this row.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a red you did not cause is a fact about main, not about your lane. Run the same witness at origin/main, cite the sha, and check this ledger before attributing it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
